I couldn't find any React code in this directory. It only holds a `.claude/skills/webgpu` skill, which doesn't apply to list rendering. If you paste the list component or point me to its path, I can make the changes directly. Until then, here are the fixes that usually help most, in rough order of impact.

### 1. Use stable, unique keys
```jsx
// Bad: index keys make React re-render or remount rows when the list is reordered, filtered or added to
{items.map((item, i) => <Row key={i} item={item} />)}

// Good
{items.map(item => <Row key={item.id} item={item} />)}
```

### 2. Memoize the row component
```jsx
const Row = React.memo(function Row({ item, onSelect }) {
  return <li onClick={() => onSelect(item.id)}>{item.name}</li>;
});
```
`React.memo` only helps if the props stay the same between renders, which leads to #3.

### 3. Keep props stable
New functions, objects or arrays created during render break `memo`:
```jsx
// Bad: a new function and a new style object on every render
<Row item={item} onSelect={() => select(item.id)} style={{ color: 'red' }} />

// Good
const handleSelect = useCallback(id => select(id), [select]);
<Row item={item} onSelect={handleSelect} />   // move static styles to a constant outside the component
```
If you use the **React Compiler** (React 19+), it adds this memoization for you, so you can skip most manual `memo` and `useCallback`.

### 4. Don't recompute derived data on every render
```jsx
const visible = useMemo(
  () => items.filter(i => i.name.includes(query)).sort(byDate),
  [items, query]
);
```

### 5. Keep state close to where it's used
If typing in a search box or hovering a row re-renders the whole list, move that state into a child component. Also avoid one big context value that changes often and that every row reads. Split it into smaller contexts, or pass each row only the data it needs (for example `isSelected={selectedId === item.id}` instead of `selectedId`).

### 6. Virtualize long lists
With hundreds or thousands of rows, render only what's on screen:
```jsx
import { useVirtualizer } from '@tanstack/react-virtual';
// or react-window's <FixedSizeList> / <VariableSizeList>
```
Above roughly 500 rows, this usually helps more than everything else combined.

### 7. Keep input responsive while the list updates
```jsx
const deferredQuery = useDeferredValue(query);
const visible = useMemo(() => filter(items, deferredQuery), [items, deferredQuery]);
```

### Measure first
Turn on "Highlight updates when components render" in React DevTools, then record in the **Profiler** tab. That shows which rows re-render and why ("props changed: onSelect"), so you only fix what's actually slow.

